prompt: An adventurer strolling through the village to replenish his gear.
answers:
   -  some market stalls from local farmers selling all sorts of fruits, vegetables, fish and meat. The market stall owners tend to chat with each other between selling their goods, thus providing tidbits of local gossip
   -  a wandering tinker, looking a bit shady yet ready to  sharpen your  knifes and daggers
   -  the local blacksmith, more used to repair farming tools and nail on horseshoes than smithing pieces of armor, but nevertheless does his best
   -  a general goods store, where you may find more obscure wares. The owner is an equally obscure male gnome, ready to earn as much coin as possible
   -  the local healer shop, owned by an old witch. She looks more frightening than she actually is, and  customers who treat her with respect will find help for all ailments
   -  an elven couple serving as tailors, stranded here from a faraway land after some rumored scandal at a royal court. They are both snobbish and expensive, but make exquisite clothes
   -  a grumpy dwarf working as jeweller and part time weapon smith
   -  a very shady looking mage shop owned by a Tiefling mage, playing into his act of evil wizard just to deter any  casual thieves
